# BeeShell basics on the RAM disk: echo, quoting, help, errors.
$ echo hello bee
hello bee
$ echo "two  spaces"   kept
two  spaces kept
$ echo "unclosed
missing closing quote
$ help
~ ^\s+help\s+show this help
~ ^\s+selftest\s+run the kernel self-tests
~ ^\s+reboot, shutdown
$ frobnicate
frobnicate: command not found (type 'help')
$ cat
cat: wrong arguments (see 'help')
$ exit
BeeShell is the system console; use 'shutdown' or 'reboot'.
$ pwd
/
